{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Inclusion criteria were as follows: (i) randomised controlled trials (RCTs), (ii) studies comparing 3D printing-assisted surgery to conventional surgery, (iii) treatment of fractures of the foot and/or ankle, (iv) published in 2012 or later, (v) outcome measures include at least 2 of: intraoperative blood loss, operation duration and fluoroscopy time. The following exclusion criteria were applied: (i) any other study type, (ii) non-English language, (iii) non-human studies, (iv) cadaveric studies, (v) studies investigating primarily patients with pathologies other than trauma (e.g. tumours, osteoporosis), (vi) studies published before 2012.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies study design (RCTs), population (foot/ankle fracture patients), intervention/comparator, outcome requirements and publication year cutoff, and lists multiple exclusion types. It does not fully specify other study characteristics such as settings or follow-up requirements for eligibility (e.g. minimum follow-up is not given in this section), so this is partial."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "All searches were restricted to English language only and a publication date of 2012 or later.",
      "reason": "The review explicitly states language and dissemination year restrictions. It does not clearly state any restriction or criteria regarding publication or report status (e.g. inclusion/exclusion of unpublished reports or preprints) beyond conducting a grey literature search, so the element is only partially satisfied."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_12",
      "quote": \"Yang et al. (2016) recorded an operation duration of 71 ± 23 min and 98 ± 20 min in the 3D and control groups respectively ( p = < 0.05) (Table 2). ... Neither the number of times fluoroscopy was used nor AOFAS score were reported in this study [32]. ... a meta-analysis of AOFAS score (Fig. 6) also excluded the study by Yang et al. [32] due to a lack of data.\",
      "reason": "The review notes that a particular study did not report certain outcomes and that it was excluded from a meta-analysis due to lack of data, indicating some distinction between non-reporting and exclusion. However, there is no systematic statement or general approach explicitly distinguishing exclusion because outcomes were not measured versus not reported across studies, so this is partial."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": \"A metaanalysis of a subgroup of studies that reported quantitative data for the outcomes: operation duration, intraoperative blood loss, number of times fluoroscopy was used, and American Orthopaedic Foot and Ankle Society (AOFAS) Ankle-Hindfoot Rating System scores in control and 3D printing intervention groups were conducted in RevMan 5.3 (Cochrane Informatics & Technology), using the dichotomous data function, and employing a random effects model.\",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies the groups used in the syntheses (control and 3D printing intervention groups) and links these to the comparisons for the specified outcomes included in the meta-analyses."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No explicit rationale is provided for notable eligibility restrictions (e.g. choice of 2012 as the publication year cutoff or the English-language restriction). The text gives background motivation for the review focus but does not justify these specific restrictions."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 80
}

